Z||000000||fiero56||12-14-2000||10:34 PM||||I am thinking about the stereo in my Formula again. I really like the 6x9s in the dash, they sound great. Now I am thinking about the rear speakers. 4x6 is nice, but I'm wondering about the possibility of installing something a little bigger. A 6 1/2" 2-way speaker actually. I don't care how it is mounted, but have 2 requirements: <BR>1)It must be mounted in such a way that it is solidly mounted and doesn't rattle.<BR>2)It must preserve the stock appearance of the b-pillar trim and grill.<P>Any ideas on this experiment? My biggest concern is speaker depth. The speakers I have my eye on require 54mm(2 1/8")depth.<P>Edited because I can't count.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||varnster||12-15-2000||07:31 PM||||Check out the infinity 4x6 at Circuit city<BR>they are white, man are they CLEANNNNNN.<BR>when you here them you will shop around no<BR>more. I heard a set in a new s-10 the guy<BR>was using a ALPINE head unit 60x4 no amp<BR>and I fell in love!||||reg||1
