Z||000003||fiero56||12-18-2000||01:05 AM||||I've heard those Infinities before. They are my back-up choice at the moment. The 6 1/2" speakers I have my eye on actually provide better highs than the Infinity plates, and also provide for a little more bass. My plan is by the time the stereo is finished I won't need a sub. That's the plan at least. Right now, the 6x9s are nice(many times better than 4x10s), but not enough. I am hoping by the time I get the 6 1/2" speakers in, and an aftermarket headunit, there will be more than enough music for my taste. Right now, the factory unit doesn't provide enough power for the 6x9s, sound is distorted pretty easily anytime I turn the bass up 3/4 and have the volume any higher than moderate, but its enough to make the inside rearview mirror shake from the bass.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
